{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 124, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring the input-output residual from nothing is a large gain, while replacing an existing conv on edge 3 gains little or loses accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is empty the output relies more on the edge-3 skip, so removing it is much more damaging and can disconnect the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pool with a learnable conv on the path feeding node 1 yields a larger gain than replacing other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 removed, node 2 has fewer or no inputs, so a conv on edge 5 has little signal to process."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a pooling path where there was none is better than replacing a useful conv or skip with pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv3x3 with pooling on node 1's only input removes learnable capacity and hurts more than replacing weaker ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pooling-heavy cells have almost no learnable capacity, so adding a conv gives a proportionally larger improvement."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 is empty, so edge 4 carries nothing and the conv contributes nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none